<title>FRANCE: French July adjusted trade surplus 11.10 bln Ffr.</title>
<headline>French July adjusted trade surplus 11.10 bln Ffr.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-09-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>France had a seasonally adjusted trade surplus in July of 11.104 billion francs compared with a revised surplus in June of 9.781 billion, provisional customs office data showed.</p>
<p>The office had originally reported a surplus in June of 9.75 billion francs.  </p>
<p>Detailed figures, in billions of francs and seasonally adjusted unless otherwise stated, were as follows:</p>
<p>					   July     June</p>
<p> Trade balance			11.10    9.78</p>
<p> Trade balance (unadjusted)     13.53   11.17</p>
<p> Imports			     109.20  108.57</p>
<p> Exports			     120.30  118.36</p>
<p> Agri-business balance	     4.51    3.32</p>
<p> Energy balance		     -5.69   -5.84</p>
<p> Industrial/military balance     8.39    8.33</p>
<p> Airbus exports	 1.76 (5 planes)    4.46 (11)</p>
<p> Defence (unadj)		     0.56    0.61</p>
<p> Unadjusted exports		125.38  124.37</p>
<p> Unadjusted imports		111.85  113.20</p>
<p> European Union			4.38    2.71</p>
<p> Germany				 1.04    0.56</p>
<p> Japan				  -1.42   -1.04</p>
<p> United States			-2.16   -0.90</p>
<p>Cumulative figures for the first seven months of the year were as follows:</p>
<p>					Jan-July 1996     Jan-July 1995</p>
<p> Before seasonal adjustment    70.02		 62.65</p>
<p> Seasonally adjusted	     64.45		 57.63</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +33 1 4221 5381</p>
</text>
